# Secrets. Never commit these.
.env
.env.local

node_modules/
.DS_Store

# NOT ignored, deliberately:
#
#   out/              the rendered dashboards
#   site/             the packaged folder the host serves
#   data/snapshots/   the frozen weekly numbers
#   data/meetings/    the raw transcripts
#   data/manual/      numbers typed in by hand
#
# Generated files normally stay out of a repo. Here they belong in it. The
# static host serves straight from the repo, so site/ has to be committed or
# there is nothing to deploy. And the snapshots ARE the history: keeping them in
# git is what makes a past week render identically forever, and shows exactly
# when a number changed.
#
# RAW TRANSCRIPTS ARE KEPT, on purpose. They are the source the decision log is
# built from, and a log you cannot trace back to what was actually said is a log
# you end up arguing with. Two things follow from keeping them:
#
#   1. The repo must stay PRIVATE. Transcripts hold verbatim speech - candid
#      criticism, people discussed by name, things said in confidence. That is a
#      different sensitivity class from a pipeline number.
#   2. site/ never carries them. bin/build-site.js copies an allowlist of four
#      folders and data/ is not one of them, so a transcript cannot reach the
#      published URL even by accident.
